</div>
  <p>If <b>face</b> is <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/ALL_SIDES" target="_blank">ALL_SIDES</a> then the function works on all sides.</p>
  <p><b>start</b> supports <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/Category:LSL_Negative_Index" target="_blank">negative indexes</a>.</p>
  <p>Frames are numbered from left to right, top to bottom, starting at 0.</p>
  <p>If <b>rate</b> is negative, it has the same effect as using the <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/REVERSE" target="_blank">REVERSE</a> flag.[[2]](#footnote_2)</p>
  <p>If <b>length</b> is 0, it is considered to be <b>sizex</b>*<b>sizey</b> if both are above 0, otherwise 1.</p>
  <h2>Specification</h2>
  <table>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <th>Index</th>
        <th>Positive</th>
        <th>Negative</th>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>First</td>
        <td>`0`</td>
        <td>`-**length**`</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Last</td>
        <td>`**length** - 1`</td>
        <td>`-1`</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <h3>Indexes</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Positive indexes count from the beginning, the first item being indexed as `0`, the last as `(**length** - 1)`.</li>
  </ul>
  <ul>
    <li>Negative indexes count from the far end, the first item being indexed as `-**length**`, the last as `-1`.</li>
  </ul>
  <h3>Frames</h3>
  <p>Frames are sub-rectangles within the texture. A set of frames with 2 horizontal (<b>sizex</b>) and 3 vertical (<b>sizey</b>) means the overall texture is divided into 3 rows of 2 columns of images, each of which is a frame. llSetLinkTextureAnim will animate across these 6 starting with the top left image and going across and down, optionally repeating. If <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/SMOOTH" target="_blank">SMOOTH</a> is set the frames slide smoothly from one to the next, if off, each frame is displayed in turn centered on the face.</p>
  <table>
    <tbody>
